    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001V5": {
      "title": "Job Description - Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Medical Laboratory Science (N&HS)  (26001V5)",
      "description": "Job Description - Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Medical Laboratory Science (N&HS)  (26001V5) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Medical Laboratory Science (N&HS)  (26001V5) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk. We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the School of Nursing and Health Sciences: Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Medical Laboratory Science (N&HS) - ( 26001V5 ) Job : Full-time Academic School/Unit : School of Nursing and Health Sciences Closing Date : 03/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Undertaking course planning, development, coordination and delivery (including classroom and clinical teaching) in related disciplines; Participating in programme development and accreditation exercise; Performing scholarly activities and increasing the publication output and raising the level of consultancies in related discipline(s); Leading and promoting research and collaboration; Supervising undergraduate and postgraduate research project(s); Engaging in student development activities; and Undertaking / Participating in School / University activities and administration. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A doctoral degree in Medical Laboratory Science / Biomedical Science or a related discipline; Substantial relevant experience in clinical / teaching / research in Medical Laboratory Science in hospital or the tertiary education sector; Competence in teaching / professional experience including programme development and course administration; Strong communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction; A record of research and peer-reviewed scholarly publications; Applicants MUST hold a Part 1 registration and a valid practicing certificate with the Medical Laboratory Technologist Board of HKSAR; and Relevant and ample clinical experience in one of the following areas is desirable. o Medical Immunology o Hematology o Clinical Chemistry o Medical Microbiology The level of appointment depends on the candidate’s academic background, experience and competence in academic leadership, teaching, research, scholarly publications, etc. Candidate with less qualification and experience may be considered for appointment as Assistant Professor / Senior Lecturer Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. “Accommodation Programme for Overseas Young Teaching Staff” sponsored by the “Katie Shu Sui Pui Charitable Trust” Overseas candidates who are successfully appointed by the University and below age 50 will be eligible to apply for the “Accommodation Programme for Overseas Young Teaching Staff” sponsored by the “Katie Shu Sui Pui Charitable Trust”. This programme offers the opportunity to reside in assigned accommodation free of charge for a period of up to six months, subject to terms and conditions. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001V4": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Public Affairs Manager (Marketing) (PAO) (26001V4)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Public Affairs Manager (Marketing) (PAO) (26001V4) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Public Affairs Manager (Marketing) (PAO) (26001V4) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Public Affairs Office : Assistant Public Affairs Manager (Marketing) (PAO) - ( 26001V4 ) Job : Full-time Non-Academic School/Unit : Public Affairs Office Closing Date : 03/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The Public Affairs Office (PAO) is seeking a proactive and self-motivated candidate to assist our marketing initiatives. Reporting to the Director of Public Affairs or his/her nominee(s) in the PAO, the successful candidate will mainly be responsible for: Developing brand/marketing strategies, and executing full-funnel marketing initiatives to enhance visibility, brand awareness and student acquisition; Creating organic content (posts, visuals/photos, videos) and managing the accounts for HKMU’s social media channels, including Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn and Xiaohongshu, to support branding and student acquisition; Planning and implementing data-driven digital marketing campaigns across multiple channels, such as the websites, paid search, paid social, display and content engagement; Timely tracking and analysing marketing performance, preparing regular reports with actionable recommendations for future plans; Organising offline marketing and branding initiatives, including events and info days; Producing corporate, event and programme promotional videos with video production houses; Coordinating market research on University’s brand image and positioning; Exploring and identifying new channels and media to effectively reach target audience; and Performing other tasks as assigned by the Director of Public Affairs or his/her nominee(s). Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competencies : A recognised degree, preferably in journalism, communications, marketing, business, public relations or related disciplines; At least 5 years of relevant experience in marketing and communications, with a strong focus on social media content development and management (particularly Xiaohongshu); Experience in executing omni-channel strategies, including SEO/SEM, social media management and growth strategies, advertising campaigns and delivering measurable results; Expertise in digital marketing tools (e.g. Google Ads, Google Analytics, Meta Ads) is an advantage; Analytical mindset with the ability to interpret complex data and translate it into actionable strategies; Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese, preferably including Putonghua; Strong PR sense; Mature, detail-oriented, self-motivated, and a good team player with good interpersonal and communication skills; Well-organised with strong multi-tasking and time management skills; Capable of managing projects independently while working under pressure and tight deadlines; and Flexible and willing to work outside office hours when necessary. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and interview. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. (Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement posted in Jul 2026 need not re-apply.) The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment.  For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuc cessful."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001UB": {
      "title": "Job Description - Full-time Research Assistant II (R6A17) (A&SS) (26001UB)",
      "description": "Job Description - Full-time Research Assistant II (R6A17) (A&SS) (26001UB) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Full-time Research Assistant II (R6A17) (A&SS) (26001UB) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the School of Arts and Social Sciences : Full-time Research Assistant II (R6A17) (A&SS) - ( 26001UB ) Job : Full-time R&D School/Unit : Wu Jieh Yee School of Arts and Social Sciences Closing Date : 30/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will primarily assist the Principal Investigator, Dr Julie Liao, in coordinating a research project related to developing behavioural interventions for supporting parents’ decision making in children’s influenza vaccination and other behavioural health-related research. The appointee shall mainly be responsible for the following: Conducting comprehensive literature searches and reviews; Conducting pilot testing of the study instruments; Managing project logistics, including the coordination of part-time helpers and data collection; Cleaning and managing the dataset and performing data analysis; Assisting in the preparation of research reports, academic publications, and presentation materials; and Performing other related duties as assigned by the Principal Investigator. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: A Bachelor’s degree or above in Psychology, Social sciences, Nursing, or other health-related disciplines; Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese, Good interpersonal and communication skills; A strong sense of responsibility, and a hard-working attitude; Experience in conducting surveys and behavioural interventions, competence in quantitative data analysis, and good computer skills will be advantageous. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary and an end-of-contract gratuity, will be offered to the right candidates. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System. Please contact Dr Julie Liao by e-mail to jliao@hkmu.edu.hk for enquiries about the post. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001TN": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Professor (Department of Management and Strategy – Strategic Management / Human Resource Management / Organisational Behaviour) (B&A) (26001TN)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor (Department of Management and Strategy – Strategic Management / Human Resource Management / Organisational Behaviour) (B&A) (26001TN) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor (Department of Management and Strategy – Strategic Management / Human Resource Management / Organisational Behaviour) (B&A) (26001TN) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . About the Department of Management and Strategy The Department of Management and Strategy at the Lee Shau Kee School of Business and Administration, Hong Kong Metropolitan University is a young and vibrant department actively building a strong research team. The Department brings together a broad spread of disciplines, including business management, human resources management, aviation service management, real estate and surveying, sport and esports management, and hospitality and tourism management. It is home to the School’s MBA and DBA programmes, with the MBA being the largest MBA programme in Hong Kong. This disciplinary breadth offers rich opportunities for cross-disciplinary collaboration and for applied, industry-facing research that speaks directly to Hong Kong and the Greater Bay Area. The School provides robust research support, including internal research funding, and adopts a balanced approach to research and teaching, offering a collegial and supportive environment for early-career scholars to grow and excel. We seek promising early-career scholars who are close to completing or have recently completed a PhD and aim to build an international research reputation in strategic management, human resource management, or organisational behaviour. The appointee will contribute to teaching on the largest MBA programme in Hong Kong, alongside our undergraduate and DBA offerings. In line with our ambition to be a thought leader in the applied sciences field, our faculty members have published in many of the world’s leading academic journals, including Academy of Management Review, Strategic Management Journal, Organization Science, Journal of International Business Studies, Journal of Business Venturing, and Entrepreneurship Theory and Practice , and others. Our faculty also serve the academic community through editorial review board memberships at prestigious journals and active professional engagements. As a testament to the impact we make, our faculty members have received international awards for their research and contributions to knowledge creation. We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Lee Shau Kee School of Business and Administration : Assistant Professor (Department of Management and Strategy – Strategic Management / Human Resource Management / Organisational Behaviour) (B&A) - ( 26001TN ) Job : Full-time Academic School/Unit : Lee Shau Kee School of Business and Administration Closing Date : 18/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Undertaking/engaging in scholarly and professional activities, with a focus on building a strong research pipeline and an international research reputation; Planning, developing, coordinating, and delivering courses (including classroom teaching) in the areas of strategic management, human resource management, and business sustainability at the undergraduate and/or postgraduate levels;and Participating in School/University activities and administration. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: An earned doctorate in Strategic Management, Human Resource Management, Organisational Behaviour, or a closely related field (or be near completion at the time of appointment); A strong and promising research profile, with evidence of a high level of scholarly achievement. Competitive candidates will typically have at least one paper under “Revise & Resubmit” or at a more advanced stage in a UTD24, FT50 journal, or equivalent; A demonstrated strong research pipeline, with ongoing projects and papers under review at leading international journals (e.g., ABS 3 or above); A strong commitment to teaching excellence and the ability to teach in English at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels; and Strong communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, a composite cash/housing allowance, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidate. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System and upload the following documents: Curriculum Vitae; Job-market paper; Research statement (including publication record and pipeline); and At least three referee letters. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
    "https://hkmu.taleo.net/careersection/ex_full_time/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001TL": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Professor/ Senior Lecturer (Department of Management and Strategy – Sports Management) (B&A) (26001TL)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor/ Senior Lecturer (Department of Management and Strategy – Sports Management) (B&A) (26001TL) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor/ Senior Lecturer (Department of Management and Strategy – Sports Management) (B&A) (26001TL) Founded in 1989, Hong Kong Metropolitan University (HKMU) is a modern, vibrant and dynamic university. We tailor our professional programmes to adapt to market trends and meet industry needs, thus providing our students with quality professional education and clear career paths. Being the first University of Applied Sciences (UAS) in Hong Kong, we pledge to play a pioneering role in enhancing recognition of vocational and professional education and training, and nurturing talents with both applied skills and knowledge. As a faculty-driven, student-centred university in support of innovative teaching and learning, strategic research, and stakeholder outreach to provide maximum benefit to our communities, we conduct research that advances knowledge and enhances teaching, focusing on strategic areas, including digital humanities and literature, international business, gerontechnology, personalised care, smart city, open and innovative education, and bilingual learning and teaching. HKMU is becoming an ever more vital link in addressing and helping Hong Kong to solve many difficult challenges – as part of our involvement in, and commitment to, the ‘metropolis’ of Hong Kong. Our plans to expand into the Greater Bay Area (GBA) will also cultivate talent to serve Hong Kong and the wider metropolitan GBA. For more information about the University, please visit https://www.hkmu.edu.hk . About the Department of Management and Strategy The Department of Management and Strategy at the Lee Shau Kee School of Business and Administration, Hong Kong Metropolitan University, is a young and vibrant department actively building a strong research team. The Department brings together a broad range of disciplines, including business management, human resources management, aviation service management, real estate and surveying, sport and esports management, and hospitality and tourism management. It is home to the largest Sports and Recreation Management Programme in Hong Kong. This disciplinary breadth offers rich opportunities for cross-disciplinary collaboration and for applied, industry-facing research that speaks directly to Hong Kong and the Greater Bay Area. The School provides robust research support, including internal research funding, and adopts a balanced approach to research and teaching, offering a collegial and supportive environment for early-career scholars to grow and excel. We seek promising early-career scholars who are close to completing or have recently completed a PhD and aim to build an international research reputation in sport and esports management. The appointee will join the discipline team behind the largest Sports and Recreation Management Programme in Hong Kong. In line with our ambition to be a thought leader in the applied sciences field, our faculty members have published in many of the leading academic journals in sports and leisure management, including Journal of Sport Management , Sport Management Review , European Sport Management Quarterly, Leisure Studies, Leisure Sciences and others. Our faculty also serve the academic community through editorial boards at prestigious journals and active professional engagements. As a testament to the impact we make, our faculty members have received international awards for their research and contributions to knowledge creation. The Department offers appointees a supportive platform to develop impactful, applied research and build collaborations with industry and professional communities in Hong Kong and the Greater Bay Area. We are now looking for a suitable person to fill the following position in the Lee Shau Kee School of Business and Administration : Assistant Professor/ Senior Lecturer (Department of Management and Strategy – Sports Management) (B&A) - ( 26001TL ) Job : Full-time Academic School/Unit : Lee Shau Kee School of Business and Administration Closing Date : 18/Sep/2026, 8:59:00 AM Major Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following: Undertaking/engaging in scholarly and professional activities, with a focus on building a strong research pipeline and an international research reputation; Planning, developing, coordinating, and delivering courses (including classroom teaching) in the areas of sports and esports management at the undergraduate and/or postgraduate levels; and Participating in School/University activities and administration. Candidates Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence: An earned doctorate in sports management, or a closely related field (or be near completion at the time of appointment); A strong and promising research profile, with evidence of a high level of scholarly achievement. Competitive candidates will typically have publications in leading sport management journals (e.g., Journal of Sport Management, Sport Management Review, European Sport Management Quarterly, International Journal of Sports Marketing and Sponsorship) or journals of equivalent standing; A demonstrated strong research pipeline, with ongoing projects and papers under review at leading international journals in sports management and/or related business disciplines (e.g., management, marketing, strategy, human resource management, tourism and hospitality), including journals ranked ABS 3 or above, or equivalent. A strong commitment to teaching excellence and the ability to teach in English at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels; and Strong communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction. Terms and Conditions for Appointment An attractive remuneration package, including basic salary, a composite cash/housing allowance, an end-of-contract gratuity, and a discretionary incentive payment, where applicable, will be offered to the right candidate. Generous annual leave, staff-development sponsorships, medical and dental benefits, and life insurance coverage will also be provided. To Apply Candidates who are interested in joining us may submit their applications via the University’s eRecruitment System and upload the following documents: Curriculum Vitae; Job-market paper; Research statement (including publication record and pipeline); and At least three referee letters. The personal data collected will be used for the purpose of considering your application for employment. For details, please refer to the “Personal Data (Privacy) Notice for Job Applicant” on the University’s website. If you are not contacted by the University within eight weeks from the closing date of application, you may assume that your application was unsuccessful. The University will continue to review applications until the position(s) is/are filled."
    },
